# Absolute imports via `@/`

In `apps/app`, every local import MUST use the `@/` alias (mapped to `src/` in `tsconfig.json` and `vite.config.ts`).

## Required

- Use `@/components/...`, `@/features/...`, `@/state/...`, `@/composition/...`, etc.
- Convert parent-relative paths (`../`, `../../`) to `@/` paths.
- Convert same-directory paths (`./`) to `@/` paths as well — no `./` imports.

## Forbidden

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — parent-relative
import { App } from '../app/App';
import { downloadCoordinator } from '../network/download-coordinator';

// ❌ BAD — same-directory relative
import { LocalModelController } from './controller';
export * from './types';
```

## Allowed

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — always @/ from src root
import { App } from '@/app/App';
import { downloadCoordinator } from '@/features/network/download-coordinator';
import { LocalModelController } from '@/features/models/controller';
export * from '@/features/models/types';
```

## External packages

Package imports (`@localmed/*`, `solid-js`, etc.) are unchanged. Only paths under `apps/app/src` use `@/`.

## Alias configuration

- `apps/app/tsconfig.json` — `"@/*": ["apps/app/src/*"]`
- `apps/app/vite.config.ts` — `resolve.alias['@']` → `./src`
- `vitest.config.ts` — same `@` → `apps/app/src` alias for unit tests

## When editing

After changing imports, run `bunx biome check --write` on touched files to normalize import order.
